<para id="X39400000RB01AC" category="C" type-id="3008U" name-id="065A2-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>P0340/12</dtccode>
<dtcname>Camshaft Position Sensor Circuit</dtcname>
<subpara id="X39400000RB01AC_10" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00002QU00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>The cam position sensor system (G2+ signal) consists of a pickup coil and a timing rotor provided on the camshaft. When the camshaft rotates, the air gap between the protrusions of the timing rotor and the pickup coil changes, which changes the magnetic field and generates an electromotive force in the pickup coil.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
